commit e28f2c7243546b84f07de07c1319e55d24172c05
Author: Peter Svensson <psvensson@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Jul 4 13:58:00 2026 +0200

    fix(rebalancer): idempotent op-row inserts — lost-outcome retries converge instead of dying on UNIQUE
    
    Quest replica-operation-insert-retry-idempotency (P1, affinity-demo runs
    16-17, 2/2 modal after f870f7a0): an op-row INSERT lands, its outcome is
    lost (post-apply delivery failures are now honestly surfaced instead of
    silently acked), and the blind re-INSERT collides with 'UNIQUE constraint
    failed: replica_operations.operation_id' — wrapped as a fatal
    DISTRIBUTED_PARTICIPANT_FAILURE that killed rebalancer moves and client
    CREATE TABLE (379 UNIQUE warns / 36 fatal in run 17).
    
    Operation ids are minted once, so a same-id re-insert is always a
    lost-outcome retry. The canonical-ingress insert now rides the gateway's
    EXISTING ignoreExisting option (INSERT OR IGNORE; previously wired only by
    dynamic-config), and a zero-change collision resolves as already-applied
    ONLY through the existing authoritative visibility confirmation (CONFIRMED
    with the observed row, content-matched) — never inferred from the write
    result. Absent or content-mismatched same-id rows stay hard failures.
    replica_operations has exactly one uniqueness constraint (the PK), so
    OR IGNORE cannot absorb a legitimately-different conflicting row. The
    raw-SQL fallback lane keeps the plain INSERT (production gateways always
    expose the canonical ingress).
    
    Atomically included (run-18 witness): the CDC parameterized-INSERT
    extractor accepted only INSERT [OR REPLACE] INTO, so OR-IGNORE statements
    fell through to literal parsing and emitted CDC events whose every column
    was the string '?' (3,712 parse errors, garbage read-model rows). The
    regex now matches OR IGNORE like every sibling parser.
    
    All changes dt:proven red-on-revert; adversarially verified FAITHFUL
    (single-constraint audit, changes-signal hop-by-hop trace, other-inserter
    sweep, no coalescing race, HEAD-identical false-path behavior); scenario
    harness 3x PASS (318 guard asserts); rebalancer lane green. Live witness:
    run 18 UNIQUE collisions 379 -> 0, op completions doubled.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

